.Dd $Mdocdate: September 4 2026 $
.Dt PLDOCK.CONF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pldock.conf
.Nd layout language for
.Xr pldock 1
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr pldock 1
reads a nested box language that describes one dock rectangle and the
X clients to swallow into it.
.Ic key=value
and
.Ic key value
are both accepted.
.Ql #
starts a comment to end of line.
.Pp
The file is a single
.Ic dock { }
block.
Inside it, attributes may mix with
.Ic hbox ,
.Ic vbox ,
and
.Ic tile
children.
Several children of
.Ic dock
are wrapped in a
.Ic vbox .
.Sh DOCK ATTRIBUTES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic pos
.Ic top-left ,
.Ic top-right ,
.Ic bottom-left ,
or
.Ic bottom-right
.Pq default
on the chosen output.
.It Ic screen
.Xr xrandr 1
output:
.Ic primary
.Pq default ,
an output name such as
.Ic HDMI-1 ,
.Ic left ,
.Ic right ,
.Ic top ,
.Ic bottom ,
or a 0-based index.
Width and height fractions are relative to this output, not the
combined virtual screen.
.It Ic width
Pixels, a fraction
.Pq Ic 1/3 ,
or a percent
.Pq Ic 33%
of the output width.
.It Ic height
.Ic auto
.Pq default; from the tile tree ,
pixels, a fraction, or a percent of the output height.
.It Ic gap
Pixels between cells
.Pq default 2 .
.It Ic override
Override-redirect
.Pq default on so screen placement sticks under cwm .
.Ic override=0
or
.Ic managed
lets the window manager place the dock.
.It Ic spawn
If present,
.Xr pldock 1
forks tiles that are not already mapped.
Off by default.
.El
.Sh BOXES AND TILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic hbox { ... }
A row.
Leftover width goes to children marked
.Ic stretch ,
split by
.Ic weight
.Pq default 1 .
.It Ic vbox { ... }
A column.
Leftover height goes to
.Ic stretch
children.
Boxes may nest arbitrarily.
.It Ic tile Ar name
Swallow an existing client.
.Ar name
looks up a built-in
.Pq Ic wmclock , Ic wmapm , Ic xload , Ic xconsole
for default command, match strings, and size hint.
Any other
.Ar name
is used as both the command and the
.Dv WM_CLASS
pattern.
Matching also uses the last path component, so
.Pa /usr/local/bin/wmapm
matches
.Ic wmapm .
.It Ic plugin Ar name
Open a child window owned by
.Xr pldock 1
and draw into it.
Does not swallow or spawn a foreign client.
The first plugin is
.Ic xloadio
.Pq an xload-style strip chart .
.It Ic script Ar command
Like
.Ic plugin ,
but runs
.Ar command
.Pq quote it if it contains spaces
through
.Nm sh Fl c
and paints stdout in the cell.
Default refresh is 300 seconds.
.El
.Pp
Tile flags and attributes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic stretch
Grow on the parent box's main axis and fill the cell.
Native dockapps should omit this so they keep their size
.Pq including SHAPE holes .
.It Ic min= Ns Ar N
Floor size in pixels when stretching.
.It Ic weight= Ns Ar N
Share of leftover space
.Pq default 1 .
.It Ic cmd= Ns Qq Ar a b c
Command to spawn if
.Ic spawn
is on
.Pq default: the tile name .
.It Ic match= Ns Ar a,b
.Dv WM_CLASS
/
.Dv WM_NAME
patterns
.Pq default: the tile name .
.It Ic size= Ns Ar WxH
Native size hint before the window maps.
.It Ic refresh= Ns Ar seconds
For
.Ic script :
how often to re-run the command
.Pq default 300 .
.It Ic input= Ns Ar disk | net
For
.Ic plugin xloadio :
.Ic disk
graphs read/write bytes;
.Ic net
graphs receive/send bytes.
Default
.Ic disk .
.El
.Sh PLUGINS
.Ss xloadio
Looks like
.Xr xload 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic input=disk
Read and write from
.Dv hw.diskstats .
.Ic total
sums unique devices
.Pq softraid volumes, not their backing disks .
.It Ic input=net
Receive and send from
.Nm netstat Fl ibn
link rows, skipping
.Ic lo* ,
.Ic enc* ,
.Ic pflog* .
.It Ic input=load
Three traces: 1, 5, and 15 minute load average, each a different color.
.It Ic input=mem
Stacked RAM
.Pq wired, active, cache, free
and swap
.Pq used, free .
.It Ic style=line
History strip, overlapping traces
.Pq default for disk, net, load .
.It Ic style=bar
Current values as side-by-side bars with 1 pixel of background between them.
.It Ic style=stack
Stacked segments
.Pq default for mem; history columns or a RAM column beside a swap column .
.It Ic color0 , Ic color1 , Ic color2 , ...
Per-trace color:
.Ic green ,
.Ic yellow ,
.Ic red ,
.Ic cyan ,
.Ic orange ,
.Ic gray ,
.Ic blue ,
or
.Li 66cc66
/
.Li 0x66cc66 .
Do not use unquoted
.Li #rrggbb
.Pq # starts a comment ;
quote it:
.Ic color0="#66cc66" .
.It Ic colors=green,yellow,red
Same list in one attribute.
.El
.Pp
A tiny
.Ql <
on the left edge and
.Ql >
on the right edge cycle
.Ic total
then each volume or interface for disk/net,
.Ic line Ns / Ns Ic bar Ns / Ns Ic stack
for load, and
.Ic both Ns / Ns Ic ram Ns / Ns Ic swap
for mem.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
plugin xloadio input=load style=line color0=green color1=yellow color2=red stretch
plugin xloadio input=mem style=stack stretch
plugin xloadio input=disk style=bar colors=green,yellow stretch
.Ed
.Sh SEARCH PATH
.Xr pldock 1
loads the first file that exists:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Fl c Ar file
.It
.Ev PLDOCK_CONF
.It
.Pa ~/.config/pldock/pldock.conf
.El
.Pp
Otherwise the built-in default
.Pq same layout as the shipped example
is used.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/share/examples/pldock/pldock.conf -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/pldock/pldock.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/share/examples/pldock/pldock.conf
Example installed by
.Ic make install .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Lower right of the primary output, xconsole under a row of dockapps:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dock {
	pos     bottom-right
	screen  primary
	width   1/6
	height  auto
	gap     2

	vbox {
		hbox {
			tile wmclock
			tile wmapm
			plugin xloadio input=disk stretch
			plugin xloadio input=net stretch
		}
		tile xconsole stretch min=96
	}
}
.Ed
.Pp
Same layout on the right-hand monitor:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dock {
	pos     bottom-right
	screen  HDMI-1
	width   1/3
	height  auto

	vbox {
		hbox {
			tile wmclock
			tile wmapm
			plugin xloadio input=disk stretch
			plugin xloadio input=net stretch
		}
		tile xconsole stretch min=96
	}
}
.Ed
.Pp
A dock that is only the two I/O charts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dock {
	pos     bottom-right
	screen  primary
	width   1/4
	height  64

	hbox {
		plugin xloadio input=disk stretch
		plugin xloadio input=net stretch
	}
}
.Ed
.Pp
Fixed dockapps, then stretch charts and a clock script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hbox {
	tile wmclock width=56
	tile wmapm width=56
	plugin xloadio input=disk stretch
	plugin xloadio input=net stretch
	script "date" refresh=300 stretch
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cwm 1 ,
.Xr pldock 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1
